            <div class="post-body__intro reveal">
              <p>When it comes to designing or renovating a kitchen, bathroom, or any space that requires storage, the choice of cabinetry is often the most significant decision. The right cabinet style can completely transform a room, offering not just functionality but also an essential aesthetic that reflects the latest trends of 2026. However, with so many cabinet styles to choose from, selecting the perfect one for your space can be overwhelming.</p>
              <p>Whether you're a homeowner embarking on a renovation or a contractor guiding your clients through the design process in 2026, understanding the different cabinet styles is crucial. In this blog, we'll break down the most popular cabinet styles, the factors that influence your decision &mdash; and crucially, what Delaware County homeowners are actually choosing in 2024&ndash;2025 and why. We'll also include real cost benchmarks and first-hand installation insights from our team.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="post-body__section reveal">
              <h2>1. Understanding Cabinet Styles: What You Need to Know</h2>
              <p>Before you dive into choosing a cabinet style according to 2026 trends, it's essential to understand what different styles entail. Cabinet designs can vary widely in terms of their door style, finish, and construction. Broadly speaking, cabinets fall into one of several categories, with each offering distinct aesthetics and functionality suited to 2026 home preferences.</p>

              <h3>Shaker Style Cabinets</h3>
              <p>Shaker-style cabinets are one of the most popular choices for both modern and traditional homes in 2026. This style features a simple, clean design with a flat panel door and square edges. The minimalist nature of Shaker cabinets makes them highly versatile, fitting into a range of home styles, from rustic to contemporary. The plain design also allows for customization with different finishes and hardware, making them adaptable to many tastes.</p>

              <h3>Raised Panel Cabinets</h3>
              <p>Raised panel cabinets have a more ornate look, characterized by a door design where the center panel is slightly raised. These cabinets offer a more traditional and elegant style, often seen in classic or colonial-inspired kitchens and bathrooms. The raised panel design adds texture and depth to the cabinet, making them a statement piece in a room. If you're aiming for a luxurious or vintage feel in 2026, raised panel cabinets are a great choice.</p>

              <h3>Flat-Panel (Slab) Cabinets</h3>
              <p>For a sleek, modern look in 2026, flat-panel or slab cabinets are the go-to option. These cabinets have a solid, flat door without any frames or panels. They offer a minimalist aesthetic that complements contemporary or industrial spaces. Flat-panel cabinets are also known for their smooth finish and are often paired with modern hardware, like recessed handles or touch-latch mechanisms, for a streamlined appearance.</p>

              <h3>Inset Cabinets</h3>
              <p>Inset cabinets are a more refined option that features doors and drawers set inside the frame of the cabinet, rather than sitting on top of it. This creates a flush, precise look that exudes craftsmanship and quality. Inset cabinets tend to have a more traditional feel, though they can also work well in modern, high-end designs. They require precise construction and are typically more expensive due to the level of detail involved.</p>

              <h3>Distressed Cabinets</h3>
              <p>Distressed cabinets are designed to have an antique, worn look, and they remain a strong contender in 2026 for rustic appeal. This cabinet style is popular in rustic, farmhouse, or vintage-inspired spaces, where the charm of a "lived-in" aesthetic is desired. Distressed finishes can range from subtle wear to heavily chipped paint, and they pair well with vintage hardware. If you're going for a cozy, rustic vibe in 2026, distressed cabinetry might be your ideal choice.</p>
            </div>

